{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And every firstborn shall die.</b> Whether he is the firstborn of the man or the firstborn of the woman. And this is what David, peace be upon him, said (Psalms 78:51): ״ויך כל בכור במצרים ראשית אונים באהלי חם״, and it is written (Psalms 105:36): ״ראשית לכל אונם״ — he mentioned concerning the firstborn of the man ״ראשית לכל אונם״, and he mentioned concerning the firstborn of the woman ״ראשית אונים באהלי חם״, because the woman is called a tent, as it is said (Judges 6:5): ״הם ומקניהם יעלו ואהליהם״." "<b>From the firstborn of Pharaoh who sits on his throne to the firstborn of the maidservant.</b> He mentioned the one great in rank and the lowly and inferior one, who is in the bondage of the millstones, and they too were punished, so that they should not say their fear was overwhelming. And afterward, in the actual event, he said 'to the firstborn of the captive,' and it is all one." "<b>But.</b> I have heard a reason for the change of expression: the slaves would work at the millstones by day, and at night they would return them to the pit. Therefore here, in Moses' prophecy which took place by day, he mentioned 'the firstborn of the maidservant who is behind the millstones,' for that was the time of their labor by day; and in the actual event, which took place at midnight, he mentioned 'the firstborn of the captive who is in the dungeon house,' for at night they would return them to the pit." "<b>And every firstborn of the beast.</b> If a man sinned, what did the beast do? Because they would worship it, and when the Holy One, blessed be He, exacts punishment from a nation, He first exacts punishment from its deities. And so our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: just as punishment is exacted from the worshippers, so is punishment exacted from the worshipped."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The citation (שם עח) refers to Psalms 78, the preceding psalm reference; (שם קה) to Psalms 105; both normalized.", 2 "The lemma אבל ('but') apparently introduces a dissenting or alternative interpretation to the preceding comment; rendered as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:50.902584171Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}